window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["flask"]=[{"id":"flask-f0001","card":"q-flask-001-1-what-flask-is-and-the-project","sec":"flask-s002","q":"What is Flask?","a":"<p>A <strong>micro web framework</strong> for Python: small core, extensions added only when needed, full control over structure.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0002","card":"q-flask-001-1-what-flask-is-and-the-project","sec":"flask-s002","q":"Who created Flask, when, and how did it start?","a":"<p>Armin Ronacher created it in 2010. It started as an April Fools' joke.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0003","card":"q-flask-001-1-what-flask-is-and-the-project","sec":"flask-s002","q":"What are typical uses of Flask?","a":"<p>Blogs, REST APIs, microservices, dashboards and data-visualization apps (popular in data science).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0004","card":"q-flask-001-1-what-flask-is-and-the-project","sec":"flask-s002","q":"What are the prerequisites for the Flask course?","a":"<p>Basic Python, conceptual HTML/CSS, HTTP client-server basics, Git/Bash, and Python plus an editor plus a GitHub account.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0005","card":"q-flask-002-flask-vs-django","sec":"flask-s003","q":"Flask vs Django: how do they compare on type, size, flexibility, learning curve and ecosystem?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Flask</th><th>Django</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Type</td><td>Micro framework</td><td>Full-stack framework</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Size</td><td>Minimal, build only what you need</td><td>Admin, auth, ORM out of the box</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Flexibility</td><td>You choose structure and components</td><td>Convention over configuration</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Learning curve</td><td>Gentler</td><td>Steeper, powerful for enterprise</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Ecosystem</td><td>Smaller, growing</td><td>Larger, many reusable apps</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0006","card":"q-flask-002-flask-vs-django","sec":"flask-s003","q":"When should you use Flask?","a":"<p>For small/medium apps, when you want flexibility and control, for prototypes/MVPs, microservices, and charts and dashboards.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0007","card":"q-flask-002-flask-vs-django","sec":"flask-s003","q":"When should you use Django instead of Flask?","a":"<p>For large complex apps, when you want built-in auth/admin/CMS, for teams wanting convention, high-traffic apps, and strong built-in security.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0008","card":"q-flask-002-flask-vs-django","sec":"flask-s003","q":"What analogy contrasts Flask with Django?","a":"<p>Flask is a blank canvas. Django is a paint-by-numbers kit.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0009","card":"q-flask-003-project-health-tracker-dashboard","sec":"flask-s004","q":"What does the Health Tracker Dashboard let users do?","a":"<p>Enter daily exercise, meditation and sleep and track progress over time.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0010","card":"q-flask-003-project-health-tracker-dashboard","sec":"flask-s004","q":"Which technology implements each feature of the Health Tracker Dashboard?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Implementation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Templates</td><td>HTML with Jinja, template inheritance</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Forms</td><td>Flask-WTF with validation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Database</td><td>SQLite + SQLAlchemy models (dev), PostgreSQL (deployment)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>CRUD</td><td>Create, Read, Update, Delete</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Visualization</td><td>Chart.js bar charts</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0011","card":"q-flask-003-project-health-tracker-dashboard","sec":"flask-s004","q":"What is the build order of the Health Tracker project?","a":"<p>App + homepage, templates with inheritance, forms + validation, SQLite + models, CRUD, Chart.js, deploy with PostgreSQL.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0012","card":"q-flask-003-project-health-tracker-dashboard","sec":"flask-s004","q":"What is the app flow of the Health Tracker?","a":"<p>Homepage -&gt; Form (submit health data) -&gt; Database -&gt; Dashboard (charts).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0013","card":"q-flask-004-2-environment-setup-and-first-app","sec":"flask-s005","q":"What is <code>venv</code> in Python, and why use it for Flask?","a":"<p>It is built into Python 3.3+ and isolates project dependencies. Always use one.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0014","card":"q-flask-004-2-environment-setup-and-first-app","sec":"flask-s005","q":"Which commands create a venv, activate it and install Flask?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>mkdir my_first_flask_app\ncd my_first_flask_app\npython3 -m venv venv        # macOS/Linux\npython -m venv venv         # Windows\nsource venv/bin/activate    # macOS/Linux\nvenv\\Scripts\\activate       # Windows\npip install Flask</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0015","card":"q-flask-004-2-environment-setup-and-first-app","sec":"flask-s005","q":"How do you know a venv is active?","a":"<p><code>(venv)</code> appears in the prompt.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0016","card":"q-flask-004-2-environment-setup-and-first-app","sec":"flask-s005","q":"What does the first Flask <code>app.py</code> look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from flask import Flask\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(&quot;/&quot;)\ndef hello():\n    return &quot;Hello World&quot;\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    app.run(debug=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0017","card":"q-flask-004-2-environment-setup-and-first-app","sec":"flask-s005","q":"What do <code>Flask(__name__)</code>, <code>@app.route(\"/\")</code>, <code>def hello()</code>, <code>if __name__ == \"__main__\"</code> and <code>app.run(debug=True)</code> do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Line</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>Flask(__name__)</code></td><td>Create the app instance; <code>__name__</code> tells Flask where to find resources</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>@app.route(\"/\")</code></td><td>Decorator mapping the home URL to the function below</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>def hello()</code></td><td>View function</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>if __name__ == \"__main__\"</code></td><td>Run only when executed directly, not imported</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>app.run(debug=True)</code></td><td>Dev server with auto-reload on code changes</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0018","card":"q-flask-004-2-environment-setup-and-first-app","sec":"flask-s005","q":"How do you run the first Flask app and where do you open it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python3 app.py     # then open http://127.0.0.1:5000/</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0019","card":"q-flask-004-2-environment-setup-and-first-app","sec":"flask-s005","q":"How do you clone the course repo and install all its dependencies?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>git clone &lt;repo-url&gt;\ncd &lt;repo-directory&gt;\npython3 -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements.txt</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0020","card":"q-flask-005-project-structure","sec":"flask-s006","q":"What is the project structure of the Flask health tracker?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>health_tracker/\n├── app.py              # Flask app instance + routes\n├── seed.py             # Seeds DB with demo data\n├── static/             # CSS, JavaScript\n├── templates/          # index.html, form.html, dashboard.html\n└── *.db                # SQLite database (generated)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0021","card":"q-flask-006-routes-and-view-functions","sec":"flask-s007","q":"What is a Flask route and what is a view function?","a":"<p>A <strong>route</strong> maps a URL to a Python function via <code>@app.route()</code>. A <strong>view function</strong> runs when the route is hit and does the work: return HTML, render a template, redirect, query a database.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0022","card":"q-flask-006-routes-and-view-functions","sec":"flask-s007","q":"Can a Flask view return HTML directly?","a":"<p>Yes. A view can return an HTML string, for example <code>return \"&lt;h1&gt;Welcome to My Blog&lt;/h1&gt;\"</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0023","card":"q-flask-006-routes-and-view-functions","sec":"flask-s007","q":"How do you serve an HTML file from <code>templates/</code> in Flask instead of a raw string?","a":"<p>Use <code>render_template(\"index.html\")</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0024","card":"q-flask-007-url-parameters","sec":"flask-s008","q":"Why does a static route per item not scale in Flask?","a":"<p>Each item needs its own route: a route like <code>/post/1</code> serves only post 1, so <code>/post/2</code> and <code>/post/3</code> would need their own routes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/post/1&quot;)           # only post 1; /post/2, /post/3 would need their own routes\ndef show_post():\n    post = posts[1]\n    return f&quot;&lt;p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;{post[&#x27;title&#x27;]}&lt;/h2&gt;{post[&#x27;content&#x27;]}&lt;/p&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0025","card":"q-flask-007-url-parameters","sec":"flask-s008","q":"How does a Flask URL parameter handle many posts with one route?","a":"<p>It captures a path variable.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/post/&lt;int:post_id&gt;&quot;)\ndef show_post(post_id):\n    post = posts.get(post_id)\n    if not post:\n        return &quot;404: Post Not Found&quot;, 404\n    return f&quot;&lt;p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;{post[&#x27;title&#x27;]}&lt;/h2&gt;{post[&#x27;content&#x27;]}&lt;/p&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0026","card":"q-flask-007-url-parameters","sec":"flask-s008","q":"What does <code>&lt;int:post_id&gt;</code> do in a Flask route?","a":"<p>It captures an integer, validates the type, and passes it to the view as <code>post_id</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0027","card":"q-flask-007-url-parameters","sec":"flask-s008","q":"Why use <code>posts.get()</code> instead of <code>posts[...]</code> in a Flask view?","a":"<p><code>posts.get()</code> returns <code>None</code> instead of raising <code>KeyError</code>. Always handle missing data with a 404.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0028","card":"q-flask-007-url-parameters","sec":"flask-s008","q":"Which Flask URL converters exist and what do they accept?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Converter</th><th>Accepts</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>string</code></td><td>Any text without slashes (default)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>int</code></td><td>Positive integers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>float</code></td><td>Positive floating-point values</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>path</code></td><td>Like string but includes slashes</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0029","card":"q-flask-008-the-three-project-routes-app-py","sec":"flask-s009","q":"What do the three routes of the health tracker <code>app.py</code> look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from flask import Flask, render_template, request, redirect, url_for\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(&quot;/&quot;)\ndef index():\n    return render_template(&quot;index.html&quot;)\n\n@app.route(&quot;/form&quot;, methods=[&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;POST&quot;])\ndef form():\n    if request.method == &quot;POST&quot;:\n        # Process form data (to be implemented)\n        return redirect(url_for(&quot;dashboard&quot;))\n    return render_template(&quot;form.html&quot;)\n\n@app.route(&quot;/dashboard&quot;)\ndef dashboard():\n    return render_template(&quot;dashboard.html&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0030","card":"q-flask-008-the-three-project-routes-app-py","sec":"flask-s009","q":"What do <code>render_template()</code>, <code>request</code>, <code>redirect()</code> and <code>url_for()</code> do in Flask?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>render_template()</code></td><td>Render HTML from <code>templates/</code> combined with data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>request</code></td><td>Incoming request data: method, form, query params, headers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>redirect()</code></td><td>Tell the client to go to another URL</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>url_for()</code></td><td>Build a URL from a <strong>view function name</strong> (no <code>.html</code>)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0031","card":"q-flask-008-the-three-project-routes-app-py","sec":"flask-s009","q":"How can one Flask route show an empty form and process a submission?","a":"<p>Use <code>methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\"]</code>. GET shows the empty form and POST processes the data. <code>request.method</code> tells which.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0032","card":"q-flask-008-the-three-project-routes-app-py","sec":"flask-s009","q":"What is POST-Redirect-GET in Flask?","a":"<p>After a POST, redirect so a refresh does not resubmit.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0033","card":"q-flask-008-the-three-project-routes-app-py","sec":"flask-s009","q":"What is the difference between <code>url_for()</code> and <code>render_template()</code> arguments in Flask?","a":"<p><code>url_for()</code> takes the function name. <code>render_template()</code> takes the filename. Keep route paths and function names matching (<code>/form</code> -&gt; <code>form()</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0034","card":"q-flask-009-4-jinja-templating-and-inheritance","sec":"flask-s010","q":"What is Jinja, and what do <code>{{ }}</code> and <code>{% %}</code> mean?","a":"<p>Jinja is Flask's templating engine. <code>{{ }}</code> is an <strong>expression</strong> (display a value). <code>{% %}</code> is a <strong>statement</strong> (logic and control flow).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0035","card":"q-flask-010-passing-data-to-a-template","sec":"flask-s011","q":"How do you pass variables from a Flask view to a Jinja template?","a":"<p>Pass them as keyword arguments to <code>render_template</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/&quot;)\ndef index():\n    user = {&quot;username&quot;: &quot;Natasha&quot;}\n    return render_template(&quot;index.html&quot;, title=&quot;Home&quot;, user=user)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0036","card":"q-flask-010-passing-data-to-a-template","sec":"flask-s011","q":"How does a Jinja template show the <code>title</code> and <code>user.username</code> variables?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;title&gt;{{ title }}&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;h1&gt;Welcome, {{ user.username }}!&lt;/h1&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0037","card":"q-flask-011-loops-conditionals-filters","sec":"flask-s012","q":"How do you pass a list to a Flask template?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>items = [&quot;Exercise&quot;, &quot;Meditation&quot;, &quot;Sleep&quot;]\nreturn render_template(&quot;index.html&quot;, items=items)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0038","card":"q-flask-011-loops-conditionals-filters","sec":"flask-s012","q":"How do you write a loop and a conditional in Jinja?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;ul&gt;\n{% for item in items %}\n    &lt;li&gt;{{ item }}&lt;/li&gt;\n{% endfor %}\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n\n{% if user.is_admin %}\n    &lt;p&gt;Welcome, Admin!&lt;/p&gt;\n{% else %}\n    &lt;p&gt;Welcome, User!&lt;/p&gt;\n{% endif %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0039","card":"q-flask-011-loops-conditionals-filters","sec":"flask-s012","q":"What are Jinja filters, and which do <code>upper</code>, <code>lower</code> and <code>capitalize</code> give for \"Natasha\"?","a":"<p>Filters (pipe <code>|</code>) transform a value inline.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{{ user.username | upper }}       &lt;!-- NATASHA --&gt;\n{{ user.username | lower }}       &lt;!-- natasha --&gt;\n{{ user.username | capitalize }}  &lt;!-- Natasha --&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0040","card":"q-flask-012-template-inheritance","sec":"flask-s013","q":"What is Jinja template inheritance and why use it?","a":"<p>A <strong>base template</strong> holds the shared layout. Child templates <code>{% extends %}</code> it and override named <code>{% block %}</code>s. Edit the layout once and every page changes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0041","card":"q-flask-012-template-inheritance","sec":"flask-s013","q":"What does the Flask <code>base.html</code> with Bootstrap look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;link href=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css&quot; rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;{{ url_for(&#x27;static&#x27;, filename=&#x27;css/style.css&#x27;) }}&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;{% block title %}Health Tracker{% endblock %}&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;header&gt;&lt;!-- Navigation --&gt;&lt;/header&gt;\n    &lt;main class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;\n        {% block content %}{% endblock %}\n    &lt;/main&gt;\n    &lt;footer&gt;&lt;!-- Footer --&gt;&lt;/footer&gt;\n    &lt;script src=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0042","card":"q-flask-012-template-inheritance","sec":"flask-s013","q":"How does a child template such as <code>index.html</code> use <code>base.html</code> in Flask?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% extends &quot;base.html&quot; %}\n{% block title %}Home - Health Tracker{% endblock %}\n{% block content %}\n    &lt;h1&gt;Welcome to the Health Tracker Dashboard&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Track your daily exercise, meditation, and sleep.&lt;/p&gt;\n{% endblock %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0043","card":"q-flask-012-template-inheritance","sec":"flask-s013","q":"Where does custom styling go in the Flask project, and what does it do?","a":"<p>In <code>static/css/style.css</code>, to override Bootstrap.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">CSS</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>.btn-primary {\n    background-color: #your-color;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0044","card":"q-flask-012-template-inheritance","sec":"flask-s013","q":"How do you link a static CSS file in a Flask template?","a":"<p>Use <code>url_for('static', filename='css/style.css')</code>, which links static files correctly. <code>{% block content %}</code> is the overridable area.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0045","card":"q-flask-013-5-forms-with-flask-wtf","sec":"flask-s014","q":"What is Flask-WTF?","a":"<p>It wraps WTForms: forms are Python classes, with validation and CSRF protection built in.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0046","card":"q-flask-013-5-forms-with-flask-wtf","sec":"flask-s014","q":"What are the steps to add a Flask-WTF form?","a":"<p>Install (<code>pip install flask-wtf</code>), define the form class, set up a route, create the template, handle submission and validation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0047","card":"q-flask-014-define-route-render","sec":"flask-s015","q":"How do you define a Flask-WTF form with required name and email?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from flask_wtf import FlaskForm\nfrom wtforms import StringField, SubmitField\nfrom wtforms.validators import DataRequired, Email\n\nclass MyForm(FlaskForm):\n    name = StringField(&quot;Name&quot;, validators=[DataRequired()])\n    email = StringField(&quot;Email&quot;, validators=[DataRequired(), Email()])\n    submit = SubmitField(&quot;Submit&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0048","card":"q-flask-014-define-route-render","sec":"flask-s015","q":"How does a Flask route handle a Flask-WTF form, and what is <code>SECRET_KEY</code> for?","a":"<p><code>SECRET_KEY</code> is required for CSRF protection.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app.config[&quot;SECRET_KEY&quot;] = &quot;your-secret-key&quot;   # required for CSRF protection\n\n@app.route(&quot;/form&quot;, methods=[&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;POST&quot;])\ndef form():\n    form = MyForm()\n    if form.validate_on_submit():\n        username = form.name.data\n        email = form.email.data\n        return render_template(&quot;success.html&quot;, username=username, email=email)\n    return render_template(&quot;form.html&quot;, form=form)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0049","card":"q-flask-014-define-route-render","sec":"flask-s015","q":"How does a Flask-WTF form template render fields?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot;&gt;\n    {{ form.hidden_tag() }}\n    {{ form.name.label }}\n    {{ form.name(size=20) }}\n    {{ form.email.label }}\n    {{ form.email(size=30) }}\n    {{ form.submit() }}\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0050","card":"q-flask-014-define-route-render","sec":"flask-s015","q":"What does the success template of the Flask-WTF form show?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;h1&gt;Success!&lt;/h1&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Hello, {{ username }}. We&#x27;ve received your email: {{ email }}.&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0051","card":"q-flask-014-define-route-render","sec":"flask-s015","q":"What do <code>StringField</code>, <code>SubmitField</code> and <code>{{ form.hidden_tag() }}</code> do in Flask-WTF?","a":"<p><code>StringField</code> / <code>SubmitField</code> render <code>&lt;input type=\"text\"&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;input type=\"submit\"&gt;</code>. <code>{{ form.hidden_tag() }}</code> renders the hidden CSRF token field, which is essential for security.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0052","card":"q-flask-014-define-route-render","sec":"flask-s015","q":"What do <code>{{ form.name.label }}</code>, <code>{{ form.name(size=20) }}</code> and <code>form.field.data</code> do?","a":"<p><code>{{ form.name.label }}</code> renders the <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>. <code>{{ form.name(size=20) }}</code> renders the <code>&lt;input&gt;</code>, and keyword arguments become HTML attributes. <code>form.field.data</code> is the submitted value.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0053","card":"q-flask-014-define-route-render","sec":"flask-s015","q":"When does <code>form.validate_on_submit()</code> return True?","a":"<p>Only if the request is POST <strong>and</strong> all validators pass.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0054","card":"q-flask-014-define-route-render","sec":"flask-s015","q":"What is the flow of a Flask-WTF form from GET to POST?","a":"<p>GET <code>/form</code> shows the empty form. POST runs <code>validate_on_submit()</code>: valid renders <code>success.html</code>, invalid re-renders <code>form.html</code> with error messages.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0055","card":"q-flask-015-common-validators","sec":"flask-s016","q":"Which common WTForms validators exist and what do they check?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Validator</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>DataRequired()</code></td><td>Not empty, not whitespace only</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>InputRequired()</code></td><td>Some input present (even whitespace)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>Email()</code></td><td>Valid email format</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>NumberRange(min, max)</code></td><td>Number within a range</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0056","card":"q-flask-015-common-validators","sec":"flask-s016","q":"<code>DataRequired()</code> vs <code>InputRequired()</code> in WTForms?","a":"<p><code>DataRequired()</code> rejects empty and whitespace-only input. <code>InputRequired()</code> only needs some input present, even whitespace.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0057","card":"q-flask-016-project-health-data-form","sec":"flask-s017","q":"How is the <code>HealthDataForm</code> defined in the Flask health tracker?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from flask_wtf import FlaskForm\nfrom wtforms import IntegerField, DateField, SubmitField\nfrom wtforms.validators import InputRequired, NumberRange\n\nclass HealthDataForm(FlaskForm):\n    date = DateField(&quot;Date&quot;)\n    exercise = IntegerField(&quot;Exercise (minutes)&quot;, validators=[InputRequired(), NumberRange(min=0)])\n    meditation = IntegerField(&quot;Meditation (minutes)&quot;, validators=[InputRequired(), NumberRange(min=0)])\n    sleep = IntegerField(&quot;Sleep (hours)&quot;, validators=[InputRequired(), NumberRange(min=0, max=24)])\n    submit = SubmitField(&quot;Submit&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0058","card":"q-flask-016-project-health-data-form","sec":"flask-s017","q":"What do <code>IntegerField</code> and <code>DateField</code> do in the health data form, and what limit applies to sleep?","a":"<p><code>IntegerField</code> enforces numeric input and <code>DateField</code> handles dates. Sleep is limited to 0-24.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0059","card":"q-flask-016-project-health-data-form","sec":"flask-s017","q":"How does the <code>/form</code> route of the health tracker extract data before the DB step?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/form&quot;, methods=[&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;POST&quot;])\ndef form():\n    form = HealthDataForm()\n    if form.validate_on_submit():\n        date = form.date.data\n        exercise = form.exercise.data\n        meditation = form.meditation.data\n        sleep = form.sleep.data\n        # Store in database (next step)\n        return redirect(url_for(&quot;dashboard&quot;))\n    return render_template(&quot;form.html&quot;, form=form)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0060","card":"q-flask-016-project-health-data-form","sec":"flask-s017","q":"How does the health data form template show per-field errors with Bootstrap classes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% extends &quot;base.html&quot; %}\n{% block content %}\n&lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot;&gt;\n    {{ form.hidden_tag() }}\n    &lt;div class=&quot;mb-3&quot;&gt;\n        {{ form.exercise.label(class=&quot;form-label&quot;) }}\n        {{ form.exercise(class=&quot;form-control&quot;) }}\n        {% for error in form.exercise.errors %}\n            &lt;span class=&quot;text-danger&quot;&gt;{{ error }}&lt;/span&gt;\n        {% endfor %}\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    {{ form.submit(class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;) }}\n&lt;/form&gt;\n{% endblock %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0061","card":"q-flask-017-6-database-operations-with-flask-sqlalch","sec":"flask-s018","q":"What does SQLAlchemy let you do, and which package do you install for Flask?","a":"<p>It lets you work with the database through Python classes instead of raw SQL. Install <code>flask-sqlalchemy</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0062","card":"q-flask-018-configuration-and-creating-the-database","sec":"flask-s019","q":"How do you configure Flask-SQLAlchemy with SQLite?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from flask import Flask\nfrom flask_sqlalchemy import SQLAlchemy\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\napp.config[&quot;SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI&quot;] = &quot;sqlite:///health_tracker.db&quot;\napp.config[&quot;SQLALCHEMY_TRACK_MODIFICATIONS&quot;] = False\ndb = SQLAlchemy(app)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0063","card":"q-flask-018-configuration-and-creating-the-database","sec":"flask-s019","q":"What do <code>SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI</code> and <code>SQLALCHEMY_TRACK_MODIFICATIONS = False</code> do?","a":"<p><code>SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI</code> is the database location: <code>sqlite:///</code> for development, swapped for PostgreSQL/MySQL. <code>SQLALCHEMY_TRACK_MODIFICATIONS = False</code> skips tracking every object change (performance).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0064","card":"q-flask-018-configuration-and-creating-the-database","sec":"flask-s019","q":"How do you create the database tables from the Flask shell?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>export FLASK_APP=app.py        # macOS/Linux\nset FLASK_APP=app.py           # Windows\nflask shell\n&gt;&gt;&gt; from app import db\n&gt;&gt;&gt; db.create_all()\n&gt;&gt;&gt; exit()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0065","card":"q-flask-018-configuration-and-creating-the-database","sec":"flask-s019","q":"What does <code>db.create_all()</code> do, and when is <code>FLASK_APP</code> needed?","a":"<p><code>db.create_all()</code> creates <code>health_tracker.db</code> with all tables defined by models. <code>FLASK_APP</code> is required for <code>flask shell</code> and <code>flask run</code>. After adding a model, run it again (importing the model too, e.g. <code>from app import db, User</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0066","card":"q-flask-019-models","sec":"flask-s020","q":"What is a Flask-SQLAlchemy model?","a":"<p>A class inheriting <code>db.Model</code>. Its attributes become columns.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0067","card":"q-flask-019-models","sec":"flask-s020","q":"How do you define a <code>User</code> model with a unique email?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class User(db.Model):\n    id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True)\n    username = db.Column(db.String(80), nullable=False)\n    email = db.Column(db.String(120), unique=True, nullable=False)\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return f&quot;&lt;User {self.username}&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0068","card":"q-flask-019-models","sec":"flask-s020","q":"What do <code>db.Column</code>, <code>db.String(80)</code>, <code>primary_key=True</code>, <code>nullable=False</code>, <code>unique=True</code> and <code>__repr__</code> do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>db.Column</code></td><td>Column with type and constraints</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>db.String(80)</code></td><td>String with max length</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>primary_key=True</code></td><td>Unique row identifier</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>nullable=False</code></td><td>Cannot be empty</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>unique=True</code></td><td>No duplicates</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>__repr__</code></td><td>Readable string for debugging</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0069","card":"q-flask-020-crud-overview","sec":"flask-s021","q":"What SQLAlchemy code does each CRUD operation use, and what saves it?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>SQLAlchemy code</th><th>Saved with</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Create</strong></td><td><code>db.session.add(obj)</code></td><td><code>db.session.commit()</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Read</strong></td><td><code>Model.query.all()</code> / <code>Model.query.get(id)</code></td><td>none</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Update</strong></td><td><code>obj.field = new_value</code></td><td><code>db.session.commit()</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Delete</strong></td><td><code>db.session.delete(obj)</code></td><td><code>db.session.commit()</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0070","card":"q-flask-020-crud-overview","sec":"flask-s021","q":"What is a SQLAlchemy session?","a":"<p>SQLAlchemy's temporary workspace. Operations collect there until <code>commit()</code> writes them.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0071","card":"q-flask-021-create","sec":"flask-s022","q":"What is the flow to create a record in Flask-SQLAlchemy?","a":"<p>The form fields match the model, and the route validates and extracts data. Then it creates a new instance, calls <code>add</code>, then <code>commit</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0072","card":"q-flask-021-create","sec":"flask-s022","q":"How do you create a user from a form submission and show a success page?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/form&quot;, methods=[&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;POST&quot;])\ndef form():\n    form = MyForm()\n    if form.validate_on_submit():\n        new_user = User(username=form.name.data, email=form.email.data)\n        db.session.add(new_user)\n        db.session.commit()\n        return redirect(url_for(&quot;success&quot;, username=form.name.data, email=form.email.data))\n    return render_template(&quot;form.html&quot;, form=form)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0073","card":"q-flask-021-create","sec":"flask-s022","q":"How does the <code>success</code> route read values passed through the URL, and what is <code>request.args</code>?","a":"<p><code>request.args</code> is a dict-like object of URL query parameters.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/success&quot;)\ndef success():\n    username = request.args.get(&quot;username&quot;)\n    email = request.args.get(&quot;email&quot;)\n    return render_template(&quot;success.html&quot;, username=username, email=email)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0074","card":"q-flask-021-create","sec":"flask-s022","q":"What happens when a repeated email is submitted with <code>unique=True</code>, and how should production code handle it?","a":"<p>It raises a \"unique constraint failed\" error. Check first in production.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>existing = User.query.filter_by(email=form.email.data).first()\nif existing:\n    # Handle duplicate (flash message, error, etc.)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0075","card":"q-flask-022-read","sec":"flask-s023","q":"How do you read all users and show them in a Flask template?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/users&quot;)\ndef users():\n    all_users = User.query.all()\n    return render_template(&quot;users.html&quot;, users=all_users)</code></pre></div>\n<p>The template is a <code>{% for user in users %}</code> loop printing <code>{{ user.username }} - {{ user.email }}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0076","card":"q-flask-023-update-and-delete","sec":"flask-s024","q":"What is the flow of Update and Delete in Flask-SQLAlchemy?","a":"<p>Update: a form with a hidden record-ID field, the route finds the record, modifies fields, commits. Delete: a button form carries the ID, the route finds the record, calls <code>delete</code>, commits.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0077","card":"q-flask-023-update-and-delete","sec":"flask-s024","q":"How do you update a user's email in a Flask route?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/users&quot;, methods=[&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;POST&quot;])\ndef users():\n    if request.method == &quot;POST&quot;:\n        user_id = request.form.get(&quot;user_id&quot;)\n        new_email = request.form.get(&quot;email&quot;)\n        user = User.query.get(user_id)\n        if user:\n            user.email = new_email\n            db.session.commit()\n    all_users = User.query.all()\n    return render_template(&quot;users.html&quot;, users=all_users)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0078","card":"q-flask-023-update-and-delete","sec":"flask-s024","q":"How do you delete a user in a Flask route?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/delete_user/&lt;int:user_id&gt;&quot;, methods=[&quot;POST&quot;])\ndef delete_user(user_id):\n    user = User.query.get(user_id)\n    if user:\n        db.session.delete(user)\n        db.session.commit()\n    return redirect(url_for(&quot;users&quot;))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0079","card":"q-flask-023-update-and-delete","sec":"flask-s024","q":"What does the <code>users.html</code> template with inline update and delete forms look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;h1&gt;Registered Users&lt;/h1&gt;\n{% for user in users %}\n&lt;div&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;{{ user.username }} — {{ user.email }}&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;!-- Update Form --&gt;\n    &lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot; action=&quot;{{ url_for(&#x27;users&#x27;) }}&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;hidden&quot; name=&quot;user_id&quot; value=&quot;{{ user.id }}&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;email&quot; name=&quot;email&quot; placeholder=&quot;New email&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Update&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n    &lt;!-- Delete Form --&gt;\n    &lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot; action=&quot;{{ url_for(&#x27;delete_user&#x27;, user_id=user.id) }}&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Delete&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n{% endfor %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0080","card":"q-flask-023-update-and-delete","sec":"flask-s024","q":"Why does a SQLAlchemy update not need <code>db.session.add()</code>?","a":"<p>SQLAlchemy tracks changes on already-loaded objects.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0081","card":"q-flask-023-update-and-delete","sec":"flask-s024","q":"How do update and delete forms pass the record ID, and which HTTP method do data-modifying Flask routes use?","a":"<p>Hidden inputs pass the record ID without showing it. Delete takes the ID from the URL. Data-modifying routes use <code>methods=[\"POST\"]</code>, never GET.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0082","card":"q-flask-024-project-healthdata-model-and-create-read","sec":"flask-s025","q":"How is the <code>HealthData</code> model defined?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class HealthData(db.Model):\n    id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True)\n    date = db.Column(db.Date, nullable=False)\n    exercise = db.Column(db.Integer, nullable=False)\n    meditation = db.Column(db.Integer, nullable=False)\n    sleep = db.Column(db.Integer, nullable=False)\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return f&quot;&lt;HealthData {self.date}&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0083","card":"q-flask-024-project-healthdata-model-and-create-read","sec":"flask-s025","q":"How do you create the <code>HealthData</code> table?","a":"<p>With <code>flask shell</code> and <code>db.create_all()</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0084","card":"q-flask-024-project-healthdata-model-and-create-read","sec":"flask-s025","q":"How does the <code>/form</code> route store a health data entry?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/form&quot;, methods=[&quot;GET&quot;, &quot;POST&quot;])\ndef form():\n    form = HealthDataForm()\n    if form.validate_on_submit():\n        new_entry = HealthData(\n            date=form.date.data,\n            exercise=form.exercise.data,\n            meditation=form.meditation.data,\n            sleep=form.sleep.data\n        )\n        db.session.add(new_entry)\n        db.session.commit()\n        return redirect(url_for(&quot;dashboard&quot;))\n    return render_template(&quot;form.html&quot;, form=form)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0085","card":"q-flask-024-project-healthdata-model-and-create-read","sec":"flask-s025","q":"How does the dashboard route read all health data?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/dashboard&quot;)\ndef dashboard():\n    all_data = HealthData.query.all()\n    return render_template(&quot;dashboard.html&quot;, data=all_data)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0086","card":"q-flask-024-project-healthdata-model-and-create-read","sec":"flask-s025","q":"What does the first version of <code>dashboard.html</code> show, before charts?","a":"<p>Plain lists, one per metric, replaced by charts later.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% extends &quot;base.html&quot; %}\n{% block content %}\n&lt;h1&gt;Your Health Dashboard&lt;/h1&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;Exercise (minutes)&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n{% for entry in data %}\n    &lt;li&gt;{{ entry.date }} — {{ entry.exercise }} minutes&lt;/li&gt;\n{% endfor %}\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n{% endblock %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0087","card":"q-flask-024-project-healthdata-model-and-create-read","sec":"flask-s025","q":"What is the end-to-end flow of the health tracker form and dashboard?","a":"<p>GET <code>/form</code>, then POST validates, creates <code>HealthData</code>, add/commit, redirect, then GET <code>/dashboard</code> queries all rows and renders.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0088","card":"q-flask-025-7-data-visualization-with-chart-js","sec":"flask-s026","q":"What is Chart.js and how do you include it in Flask pages?","a":"<p>A JavaScript charting library: a <code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code> plus a config object (<code>type</code>, <code>data</code>, <code>options</code>). Include it from a CDN in the base template so every page has it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;script src=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0089","card":"q-flask-026-seeding-demo-data","sec":"flask-s027","q":"How do you seed demo data into the health tracker DB with a route, and what is the caveat?","a":"<p>It is a one-time route. Call it once, or entries duplicate.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from datetime import datetime\n\n@app.route(&quot;/add_data&quot;)\ndef add_data():\n    demo_data = [\n        {&quot;date&quot;: &quot;2024-01-01&quot;, &quot;exercise&quot;: 30, &quot;meditation&quot;: 15, &quot;sleep&quot;: 7},\n        {&quot;date&quot;: &quot;2024-01-02&quot;, &quot;exercise&quot;: 45, &quot;meditation&quot;: 20, &quot;sleep&quot;: 8},\n        # ... more entries\n    ]\n    for item in demo_data:\n        entry = HealthData(\n            date=datetime.strptime(item[&quot;date&quot;], &quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;).date(),\n            exercise=item[&quot;exercise&quot;],\n            meditation=item[&quot;meditation&quot;],\n            sleep=item[&quot;sleep&quot;]\n        )\n        db.session.add(entry)\n    db.session.commit()\n    return &quot;Demo data has been added to the database.&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0090","card":"q-flask-026-seeding-demo-data","sec":"flask-s027","q":"What does <code>datetime.strptime(...).date()</code> do in the seeding route?","a":"<p>It converts a date string to a <code>date</code> object for the <code>Date</code> column.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0091","card":"q-flask-026-seeding-demo-data","sec":"flask-s027","q":"What does <code>seed.py</code> do and how do you run it?","a":"<p>It seeds 90 days of random exercise, meditation and sleep values. Run it once.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python seed.py</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0092","card":"q-flask-027-charting-database-data-single-chart","sec":"flask-s028","q":"How does the chart route extract plain lists from the query?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/chart&quot;)\ndef chart():\n    data = HealthData.query.all()\n    dates = [d.date.strftime(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;) for d in data]\n    exercise = [d.exercise for d in data]\n    return render_template(&quot;chart.html&quot;, dates=dates, exercise=exercise)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0093","card":"q-flask-027-charting-database-data-single-chart","sec":"flask-s028","q":"What does the <code>chart.html</code> template with a Chart.js bar chart look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;chart-container&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;canvas id=&quot;myChart&quot;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n    const ctx = document.getElementById(&#x27;myChart&#x27;).getContext(&#x27;2d&#x27;);\n    new Chart(ctx, {\n        type: &#x27;bar&#x27;,\n        data: {\n            labels: {{ dates | tojson }},\n            datasets: [{\n                label: &#x27;Exercise (minutes)&#x27;,\n                data: {{ exercise | tojson }},\n                backgroundColor: &#x27;rgba(75, 192, 192, 0.2)&#x27;,\n                borderColor: &#x27;rgba(75, 192, 192, 1)&#x27;,\n                borderWidth: 1\n            }]\n        },\n        options: { scales: { y: { beginAtZero: true } } }\n    });\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0094","card":"q-flask-027-charting-database-data-single-chart","sec":"flask-s028","q":"How do you change the Chart.js bar chart into a line chart?","a":"<p>Change <code>type: 'line'</code>, drop <code>backgroundColor</code>, and use <code>borderWidth: 2, fill: false</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0095","card":"q-flask-027-charting-database-data-single-chart","sec":"flask-s028","q":"What do the Chart.js properties <code>type</code>, <code>labels</code>, <code>datasets</code> and <code>beginAtZero</code> mean?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>type</code></td><td><code>bar</code>, <code>line</code>, <code>pie</code>, ...</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>labels</code></td><td>X-axis labels</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>datasets</code></td><td>Array of data series (<code>label</code>, <code>data</code>, colors, <code>borderWidth</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>beginAtZero</code></td><td>Y-axis starts at 0</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0096","card":"q-flask-027-charting-database-data-single-chart","sec":"flask-s028","q":"What does <code>| tojson</code> do in a Flask template with Chart.js?","a":"<p>It safely converts Python lists to JavaScript values. It is the bridge between Flask and Chart.js.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0097","card":"q-flask-027-charting-database-data-single-chart","sec":"flask-s028","q":"What do <code>getContext('2d')</code> and <code>new Chart(ctx, config)</code> do?","a":"<p><code>getContext('2d')</code> gets the drawing context. <code>new Chart(ctx, config)</code> creates the chart.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0098","card":"q-flask-028-dashboard-with-three-charts","sec":"flask-s029","q":"How does the dashboard route pass data for three charts?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&quot;/dashboard&quot;)\ndef dashboard():\n    all_data = HealthData.query.all()\n    dates = [d.date.strftime(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;) for d in all_data]\n    exercise = [d.exercise for d in all_data]\n    meditation = [d.meditation for d in all_data]\n    sleep = [d.sleep for d in all_data]\n    return render_template(&quot;dashboard.html&quot;,\n                           dates=dates, exercise=exercise,\n                           meditation=meditation, sleep=sleep)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0099","card":"q-flask-028-dashboard-with-three-charts","sec":"flask-s029","q":"What is the structure of <code>dashboard.html</code> with three charts?","a":"<p>One canvas per chart (unique ID), one <code>getContext</code> per canvas, one <code>new Chart</code> per canvas.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;canvas id=&quot;exerciseChart&quot;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;\n&lt;canvas id=&quot;meditationChart&quot;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;\n&lt;canvas id=&quot;sleepChart&quot;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n    const dates = {{ dates | tojson }};\n    const exerciseData = {{ exercise | tojson }};\n    const meditationData = {{ meditation | tojson }};\n    const sleepData = {{ sleep | tojson }};\n\n    const ctxExercise = document.getElementById(&#x27;exerciseChart&#x27;).getContext(&#x27;2d&#x27;);\n    const ctxMeditation = document.getElementById(&#x27;meditationChart&#x27;).getContext(&#x27;2d&#x27;);\n    const ctxSleep = document.getElementById(&#x27;sleepChart&#x27;).getContext(&#x27;2d&#x27;);\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0100","card":"q-flask-028-dashboard-with-three-charts","sec":"flask-s029","q":"What canvas ID, data, label and color does each dashboard chart use?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Chart</th><th>Canvas ID</th><th>Data</th><th>Label</th><th>Color (rgba)</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Exercise</td><td><code>exerciseChart</code></td><td><code>exerciseData</code></td><td>Exercise (minutes)</td><td>Teal <code>75, 192, 192</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Meditation</td><td><code>meditationChart</code></td><td><code>meditationData</code></td><td>Meditation (minutes)</td><td>Purple <code>153, 102, 255</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Sleep</td><td><code>sleepChart</code></td><td><code>sleepData</code></td><td>Sleep (hours)</td><td>Orange <code>255, 159, 64</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0101","card":"q-flask-028-dashboard-with-three-charts","sec":"flask-s029","q":"Which alpha values do the dashboard charts use for fill and border?","a":"<p>Fill uses alpha 0.2 and border uses alpha 1.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0102","card":"q-flask-029-8-deployment-to-vercel","sec":"flask-s030","q":"Why deploy Flask to Vercel?","a":"<p>Easy deployment, auto-scaling, a free tier, serverless functions and simple updates.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0103","card":"q-flask-029-8-deployment-to-vercel","sec":"flask-s030","q":"What are the steps to deploy the Flask app to Vercel?","a":"<p>Confirm <code>requirements.txt</code>, create <code>vercel.json</code> and <code>runtime.txt</code>, set up Postgres on Vercel, update the app config, set environment variables, deploy with the CLI.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0104","card":"q-flask-029-8-deployment-to-vercel","sec":"flask-s030","q":"What goes in <code>requirements.txt</code> for the deployed app, and what is <code>psycopg2-binary</code>?","a":"<p><code>psycopg2-binary</code> is the PostgreSQL adapter.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Flask\nFlask-SQLAlchemy\nFlask-WTF\nWTForms\npsycopg2-binary</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0105","card":"q-flask-029-8-deployment-to-vercel","sec":"flask-s030","q":"What does <code>vercel.json</code> contain for a Flask app?","a":"<p>The build entry point plus the Python runtime, and it routes all requests to <code>app.py</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{\n    &quot;version&quot;: 2,\n    &quot;builds&quot;: [{ &quot;src&quot;: &quot;app.py&quot;, &quot;use&quot;: &quot;@vercel/python&quot; }],\n    &quot;routes&quot;: [{ &quot;src&quot;: &quot;/(.*)&quot;, &quot;dest&quot;: &quot;app.py&quot; }]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0106","card":"q-flask-029-8-deployment-to-vercel","sec":"flask-s030","q":"What is <code>runtime.txt</code> for on Vercel?","a":"<p>It pins the Python version.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python-3.9</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0107","card":"q-flask-029-8-deployment-to-vercel","sec":"flask-s030","q":"What does the production-ready Flask <code>app.py</code> configuration look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import os\nfrom flask import Flask\nfrom flask_sqlalchemy import SQLAlchemy\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\napp.config[&quot;SECRET_KEY&quot;] = os.environ.get(&quot;SECRET_KEY&quot;, &quot;your-secret-key&quot;)\napp.config[&quot;SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI&quot;] = os.environ.get(&quot;POSTGRES_URL&quot;, &quot;sqlite:///health_tracker.db&quot;)\napp.config[&quot;SQLALCHEMY_TRACK_MODIFICATIONS&quot;] = False\ndb = SQLAlchemy(app)\n\n@app.before_first_request\ndef create_tables():\n    db.create_all()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0108","card":"q-flask-029-8-deployment-to-vercel","sec":"flask-s030","q":"How do the database and secret key settings differ locally and on Vercel?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Local</th><th>Vercel</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Database</td><td><code>sqlite:///health_tracker.db</code></td><td>PostgreSQL via <code>POSTGRES_URL</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Secret key</td><td>Hardcoded fallback</td><td><code>SECRET_KEY</code> env var</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0109","card":"q-flask-029-8-deployment-to-vercel","sec":"flask-s030","q":"What do <code>os.environ.get(name, default)</code> and <code>@app.before_first_request</code> do in the deployed app?","a":"<p><code>os.environ.get(name, default)</code> reads env vars with a local fallback, so never hardcode secrets. <code>@app.before_first_request</code> creates tables before the first request, so no manual <code>flask shell</code> is needed in production.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0110","card":"q-flask-029-8-deployment-to-vercel","sec":"flask-s030","q":"Which project files are deployed to Vercel?","a":"<p><code>app.py</code>, <code>forms.py</code>, <code>seed.py</code>, <code>requirements.txt</code>, <code>vercel.json</code>, <code>runtime.txt</code>, <code>static/css/style.css</code>, and templates <code>base/index/form/dashboard.html</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0111","card":"q-flask-030-deploying-with-the-vercel-cli","sec":"flask-s031","q":"Which commands install the Vercel CLI, log in and make a preview deployment?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>npm install vercel      # Node.js required\nvercel --version\nvercel login            # GitHub, GitLab, or email\ncd 8-3-starter          # project directory\nvercel                  # preview deployment</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0112","card":"q-flask-030-deploying-with-the-vercel-cli","sec":"flask-s031","q":"What are the prompts during the first <code>vercel</code> deployment and the answers?","a":"<p>Set up and deploy: Yes. Scope: your account. Link to existing project: No. Project name: <code>flask-health-tracker-project</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0113","card":"q-flask-030-deploying-with-the-vercel-cli","sec":"flask-s031","q":"Why does the deployed app show a server error at first, and how do you connect Postgres?","a":"<p>Storage is not connected yet. In the Vercel dashboard go to the project -&gt; <strong>Storage</strong> -&gt; <strong>Create Database</strong> -&gt; <strong>Postgres</strong> (first database is free) -&gt; <strong>Connect</strong> it to the project. Connecting auto-populates <code>POSTGRES_URL</code> and related variables.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0114","card":"q-flask-030-deploying-with-the-vercel-cli","sec":"flask-s031","q":"Which environment variables must you set on Vercel?","a":"<p><code>POSTGRES_URL</code> is auto-populated. Add <code>SECRET_KEY</code> manually with your own unique value, in Settings -&gt; Environment Variables.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0115","card":"q-flask-030-deploying-with-the-vercel-cli","sec":"flask-s031","q":"What do you do after setting the variables, and what is the state of the Postgres DB?","a":"<p>Run <code>vercel</code> again so the variables take effect, then test the preview URL (submit the form, check the dashboard). The Postgres DB starts empty. No local SQLite data carries over.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0116","card":"q-flask-030-deploying-with-the-vercel-cli","sec":"flask-s031","q":"How do you promote a Vercel preview to production?","a":"<p>Once the preview works, run:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vercel --prod</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"flask-f0117","card":"q-flask-030-deploying-with-the-vercel-cli","sec":"flask-s031","q":"What is the full Vercel deployment flow?","a":"<p><code>vercel login</code> -&gt; <code>vercel</code> (preview) -&gt; create and connect Postgres -&gt; add <code>SECRET_KEY</code> -&gt; <code>vercel</code> (redeploy) -&gt; test -&gt; <code>vercel --prod</code>.</p>","hand":true}];
